{"title":"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy the following condition:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b371e65c189b0ab26e841e29c6668556880e7f6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(130n\\right)^{50} &gt; n^{100} &gt; 2^{200} \\ \\text{?}\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df6b568b228be9bd794938ded09bbb887d48f91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 7\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 12\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 65\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"392\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1431ad346632b25a0e7b3f12ebe19723b3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms of the inequality are positive, so we may take the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th root, yielding\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ce506d0c1da0714f2cbf52acf2c37e376cfcd6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\sqrt[50]{(130n)^{50}} &gt; \\sqrt[50]{n^{100}} &gt; \\sqrt[50]{2^{200}} \\\\ \\iff &amp;130n &gt; n^2 &gt; 2^4 \\\\ \\iff &amp;130n &gt; n^2 &gt; 16.\\end{align*}\" width=\"281\" height=\"82\" />\n</p><p>Solving each part separately, while noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1431ad346632b25a0e7b3f12ebe19723b3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, therefore gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32eb0437163b394f42ccfa6bc7782222a7b99e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 &gt; 16 \\iff n &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/34096771bf92e4b8249b212799c2612c9b915172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$130n &gt; n^2 \\iff n &lt; 130$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Hence the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2a972ddc952987f08c524f16799f3832f5ce85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 &lt; n &lt; 130$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />, and therefore the answer is the number of positive integers in the open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06e3346174f6070eb320a65c700bd63b8122c655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,130)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db4377a7bfc800605101dbaae1e5310ffd4a1e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$129-5+1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"188\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A\">2005 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\